+---
+description: "Canonical React-free DSH Client assembly for authenticated Node product shells."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# `@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-client-runtime`
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+This package assembles the canonical DSH Client object graph for a Node product shell without loading React presentation packages.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+
+## Use this package
+
+Call `DshWebClient.connect()` with an HTTP IPv4-loopback origin and the authority-bound Web cookie. The runtime mounts Connection, Gateway, generated Remotes, and the Session Controller Client, then waits for the first connection generation and Session-list refresh. Consumers retain Sessions through `client.sessions.retain()` and release every reference independently. `dispose()` tears down the complete graph and multiplexed WebSocket carrier.
+
+The Node carrier sends the cookie and origin on HTTP and WebSocket requests. It rejects non-loopback origins and multiline or empty cookies. File upload is unavailable; consumers must not call `fileUpload.upload()`.
+
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as the package assembles Client services and registers no prompt, tool, or session event.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+No direct effect; invoked Host Services own any model-visible result.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- Only authenticated loopback HTTP Hosts are supported.
+- The runtime has no Node file-upload body carrier.
